// 1. Encoder φ → (μᵢ, σᵢ²) per transition; posterior via product-of-Gaussians
// 2. Sample z ~ N(μ_post, σ²_post); SAC heads consume (s, a, z), V uses detach(z)
// 3. For each meta-batch step:
// 4.   split context into halves; encode both → z_a, z_b
// 5.   $L_{\mathrm{NCE}} = \tfrac{1}{2}(\mathrm{CE}(z_a z_b^\top/\tau, I) + \mathrm{CE}(z_b z_a^\top/\tau, I))$
// 6.   reward decoder $\hat r = f(s, a, z)$,  $L_{\mathrm{rp}} = \mathrm{MSE}(\hat r, r)$  (skipped if sparse)
// 7.   total encoder loss = $L_Q + \lambda_{\mathrm{kl}} \mathrm{KL}(q\|\mathcal N(0,I)) + \lambda_{\mathrm{rp}} L_{\mathrm{rp}} + \lambda_{\mathrm{cl}} L_{\mathrm{NCE}}$
// 8. Standard SAC V/π updates with detached z; soft target update τ=0.005

// 1. Two encoders: prob_encoder → (μ, σ²) via PoG; proto_encoder → z_t per transition
// 2. For dense rewards: $z_{\mathrm{proto}} = \mathrm{mean}_t(\mathrm{proto}(c_t))$
// 3. For sparse rewards: $z_{\mathrm{proto}} = \sum_t w_t z_t / \sum_t w_t$,  $w_t = 1 + 4\,\mathrm{ReLU}(r_t)$
// 4. Sample $z_{\mathrm{stoch}} = \mu + \sigma\,\varepsilon$
// 5. Confidence: $c = \exp(-\sigma^2)$,  $z = c\cdot z_{\mathrm{stoch}} + (1-c)\,z_{\mathrm{proto}}$
// 6. Reward decoder $\hat r(s,a,z)$ trained jointly: $L_{\mathrm{rp}} = \lambda_{\mathrm{rp}}\,\mathrm{MSE}(\hat r, r)$
// 7. Encoder loss = $L_Q + \lambda_{\mathrm{kl}}\mathrm{KL}(q\|\mathcal N(0,I)) + L_{\mathrm{rp}} + \lambda_{\mathrm{align}}\|z_{\mathrm{means}} - z_{\mathrm{proto}}\|^2$

// 1. Per-transition MLP $(o,a,r) \to (\mu_t, \log\sigma_t^2)$
// 2. Posterior: $\mu = \mathrm{mean}_t \mu_t$, $\log\sigma^2 = \mathrm{mean}_t \log\sigma_t^2$
// 3. $z = \mu + e^{0.5\log\sigma^2}\,\varepsilon$
// 4. Reward decoder $\hat r = g(s,a,z)$,  $L_{\mathrm{rew}} = \mathrm{MSE}(\hat r, r)$
// 5. Encoder objective: $L_Q + \lambda_{\mathrm{kl}}\,\mathrm{KL}(q\|\mathcal N(0,I)) + 1.0\cdot L_{\mathrm{rew}}$
// 6. KL coefficient is held at config default 0.1 (despite docstring; not annealed in code)
// 7. SAC π, Q, V trained with detached z and Polyak τ=0.005
